{
  "manufacturer": "Trane",
  "manufacturer_slug": "trane",
  "model": "TCDU coolant distribution unit (data-centre liquid cooling)",
  "model_slug": "tcdu-coolant-distribution-unit",
  "short_model": "Trane TCDU",
  "aliases": [
    "TCDU",
    "Trane CDU",
    "Trane Coolant Distribution Unit",
    "DC-SVX001A"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Pump (data-centre coolant distribution unit)",
  "applies_to": "Trane Coolant Distribution Unit (TCDU) for direct-to-chip liquid cooling, as documented in IOM DC-SVX001A-EN (April 2025).",
  "summary": "Liquid-to-liquid coolant distribution unit that moves heat from a direct-to-chip server loop (TCS) to facility water (FWS) using two variable-speed pumps and a control valve. Modbus TCP exposes one block of 16-bit holding registers: pressures, flows, temperatures, pump and valve values, setpoints, sensor range states and packed status and error words.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 503
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The register list prints Modicon holding registers starting at 40001, so 40001 is wire address 0 and 40049 is wire address 48."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Installation, Operation, and Maintenance: Coolant Distribution Unit",
    "doc_number": "DC-SVX001A-EN",
    "revision_date": "2025-04",
    "url": "https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/commercial-hvac/Literature/Installation%20Operation%20and%20Maintenance/DC-SVX001A-EN_04302025.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 71 (Modbus TCP interface, port 503), pp. 98-104 (Table 34 Modbus TCP register list)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Every register is a signed 16-bit value (data type 'INT 16'). The 'Multiplier' column is the factor applied before sending (x10 means 25.3 °C is sent as 253), so scales here are 0.1 / 0.01. The manual's REST API table states the same read scales (x0.1 for temperature, percent and kW, x0.01 for pressure).",
    "Pressure units are bar gauge as printed ('barg'); flow is litres per minute ('LPM').",
    "The 23 'State' registers (40065-40087) are described only as 'per enumeration range state below', but no state table follows in this revision; their codes are left blank.",
    "The threshold pointer block (40088-40090) needs an index-to-threshold table that the register list does not include, and the threshold value's multiplier is printed as 'Varies'.",
    "Left out: spare and reserved registers (40019-40022, 40050, 40064, 40097-40101) and FWS dT limiting setpoint 40063 (printed with no multiplier, unit or description).",
    "TCS Pump 2 Pressure (40025) carries the description of pump 1 in the source; the register name says pump 2 and is used here.",
    "Register numbers are printed from 40001 in 5-digit Modicon form; the manual gives no separate offset statement, so 40001 is taken as wire address 0."
  ],
